  "methodNotes": {
    "whatWorked": [
      "Using site:starbucks.com/menu/product search to locate canonical product IDs, then fetching https://www.starbucks.com/menu/product/{id}/{hot|iced} via static web fetch.",
      "Every fetched product page rendered the full Size Options (names and exact fl oz volumes), default Grande 'What's Included' recipe (milk, shots, default syrup/sauce pump count, default toppings/drizzles), all 12 milk options, roast options, ice/foam/steamed-temp options, and Grande headline calories/sugar/fat/protein."
    ],
    "whatWasHard": [
      "Static page fetch only renders the default Grande size. Confirming Short, Tall, and Venti default shot and pump counts requires interactive browser clicks on each size button — so all non-Grande counts are left explicit null (verified: false) rather than guessed.",
      "The full 'Customize' drawer (complete list of add-on syrups, sauces, cold foams, toppings, drizzles, and max pump count) is hidden behind an interactive 'Customize' button and is not exposed in static HTML.",
      "Prices vary by US store and are not shown until a café is selected, so all basePriceBySize and upchargeAmount values are null.",
      "Two subtle drink properties appeared on live pages that we should decide how to model before Phase 2: (1) Espresso Roast choice (Blonde, Signature, Decaf, 1/2, 1/3, 2/3 Decaf — e.g., Brown Sugar Oatmilk Shaken Espresso defaults to Blonde Espresso), and (2) Shot Pull style (Ristretto vs Long Shot — Flat White defaults to Ristretto)."
    ],
    "proposedFullPullRecipe": "Keep static fetch for rapid catalog discovery (all bases, sizes, oz, milks, and Grande recipes), then run a small targeted interactive browser pass on 1-2 representative bases per category to capture the full Customize drawer (all syrups/sauces/foams/toppings, maxCount) and confirm Short/Tall/Venti/Trenta default shot/pump patterns."
  },
